  "id": "psychosocial-development",
  "term": "psychosocial development",
  "definition": "Psychosocial development is the growth of social-emotional and related psychosocial abilities that help a person cope, support well-being, and encourage positive health behaviour. In adolescence, these abilities are also linked to reducing risk behaviour.",
